The federation completes the step it deliberately postponed. Separate party
executives surrender legal command to a common membership convention. Razem,
where present, becomes a full internal current because it has actually merged;
that status is no longer inferred from cooperation alone.

- @poland_event_queue: Continue


@federation_candidate_selection
# prose-audit: Grade A — The ballot makes the federation's prior leadership rule operational: each nomination route names who gains leverage, who pays the campaign cost and how the common candidacy survives separate party mandates.
title: Member parties select the federation's common candidate
subtitle: The leadership rule chosen in September now determines which bargains are credible.
face-image: img/poland/events/left-congress-hall.webp
new-page: true

= March 2021 — One name above several party logos

The federation needs a lead campaign candidate without pretending that person
has become leader of every member party. The September convention now matters:
a rotating presidium can rotate the candidacy, while any compact can buy a
joint primary or let party delegates settle the place privately.

- @federation_joint_primary
- @federation_rotate_candidate
- @federation_delegate_candidate


