@federation_local_integration
title: Integrate organisers without abolishing memberships
subtitle: Reciprocal organising can broaden recruitment; territorial specialisation can deepen it; parallel branches are cheaper and weaker.
new-page: true

Separate legal identities do not require separate street tables in every town.
The parties can recognise one another's organisers, divide the map by local
strength or keep parallel branches that compete for the same recruits.

- @federation_membership_passport
- @federation_local_specialists
- @federation_parallel_branches


@federation_membership_passport
title: Create a reciprocal organising passport
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Members keep their party card but may organise, recruit and vote in federal campaigns anywhere.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Shared enrolment and safeguarding need one resource.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; federation_sequence_stage = 6; federation_membership_model = "Reciprocal organising passport"; federation_route_score += 3; organiser_energy += 5; member_dues += 1; young_support += 2; movement_autonomy += 2; federation_decision_delay += 1; news_headline = "Federal members gain reciprocal organising rights without losing party identity"

The common register verifies membership without transferring it. A Razem
member can staff an SLD-held county office and a Wiosna organiser can vote in a
federal campaign meeting; each still answers to their own party on internal
policy and leadership.

- @poland_event_queue: Continue with the recruiting federation


@federation_local_specialists
title: Let each party specialise in the districts it knows
subtitle: Strong local reach and distinct identities; voters hear different Left brands across the country.
on-arrival: federation_sequence_stage = 6; federation_membership_model = "Territorial party specialisation"; federation_route_score += 2; federation_brand_dilution += 2; local_network += 6; rural_support += 2; young_support += 1; turnout_readiness += 3; media_capacity -= 1; news_headline = "Member parties divide the map by local organisational strength"

Old SLD offices rebuild county slates, Wiosna concentrates on metropolitan and
equality networks, and Razem takes organising-heavy districts. The federation
reaches places no single apparatus covers, but its leaflet changes at every
county line.

- @poland_event_queue: Continue with the specialised federation


@federation_parallel_branches
title: Keep every branch, roll and recruitment drive separate
subtitle: +1 resource. Maximum legal clarity, duplicated work and conflicting local lists.
on-arrival: resources += 1; federation_sequence_stage = 6; federation_membership_model = "Parallel member-party branches"; federation_route_score -= 2; federation_veto_pressure += 2; federation_brand_dilution += 3; organiser_energy -= 2; turnout_readiness -= 2; party_unity -= 2; news_headline = "Federal parties preserve parallel branches and competing recruitment"

No member can be moved or enrolled by another organisation. The arrangement is
cheap to administer centrally because the parties pay for it themselves. It is
expensive wherever two branches recruit the same street and draft different
candidate lists.

- @poland_event_queue: Continue with separate organisations


